From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:23:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: retry GEM allocations without compression, return
 -ENOMEM

NVKMS allocates scanout GEM objects as physically contiguous video memory.
With compression, the allocation also needs comptags and is aligned to the
compression page size. When video memory is fragmented, such an allocation
can fail although enough memory is free, and a scanout allocation has no
sysmem fallback because the display engine of a dGPU can't scan out from
system memory. Clients such as Chrome then fail to create scanout buffers,
e.g. "Cannot create bo with format=RGBA_F16 and usage=Scanout", and the
kernel log only says "Failed to allocate NVKMS memory for GEM object".

If a compressible block-linear allocation fails, retry it once without
compression before falling back to sysmem. The compressible field of the
ioctl is IN/OUT, so the caller learns that compression wasn't granted.

The ioctl also returned -EINVAL for a failed allocation, which makes
clients report "Invalid argument". Return -ENOMEM like nv_drm_dumb_create()
does, and log the size and type of the failed allocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3433796b8f12d6e725ee1cc8e36a9ba28f69baed)
---
 .../nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c  | 23 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
index 2e36323b..84a81699 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
@@ -670,6 +670,22 @@ int nv_drm_gem_alloc_nvkms_memory_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
     allocParams.compressible = &p->compressible;
 
     pMemory = nvKms->allocateMemory(nv_dev->pDevice, &allocParams);
+    if (pMemory == NULL && p->block_linear && p->compressible) {
+        /*
+         * Compressible allocations need comptags and are aligned to the
+         * compression page size, and scanout allocations must also be
+         * physically contiguous. In fragmented video memory, an uncompressed
+         * allocation can still fit. p->compressible is IN/OUT, so the caller
+         * sees that compression wasn't granted.
+         */
+        NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(
+                nv_dev,
+                "Failed to allocate compressible NVKMS video memory of size %" NvU64_fmtu " for GEM object, retrying without compression",
+                p->memory_size);
+        p->compressible = 0;
+        pMemory = nvKms->allocateMemory(nv_dev->pDevice, &allocParams);
+    }
+
     if (pMemory == NULL && (p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT)) {
         NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(
                 nv_dev,
@@ -679,9 +695,12 @@ int nv_drm_gem_alloc_nvkms_memory_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
     }
 
     if (pMemory == NULL) {
-        ret = -EINVAL;
+        ret = -ENOMEM;
         NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_ERR(nv_dev,
-                           "Failed to allocate NVKMS memory for GEM object");
+                           "Failed to allocate NVKMS memory of size %" NvU64_fmtu " for %s GEM object",
+                           p->memory_size,
+                           (p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT) ?
+                               "offscreen" : "scanout");
         goto nvkms_alloc_memory_failed;
     }
 
